This product includes software developed at
Marimo Bot (https://github.com/DevTarlow/marimo-bot).

The app downloads the following third-party artefacts on the user's machine.
They are not distributed inside this repository or inside a packaged build.

Kitten TTS 2 Mini (Spoken replies, optional)
  KittenML
  The int8 ONNX graph, the English voice pack, the vocabulary, the model
  catalogue and the converted CMU pronunciation dictionary.
  Licensed under the Apache License 2.0.
  https://huggingface.co/KittenML/kitten-tts-2-mini

  The English text front end and the normaliser in
  packages/runtime/src/speech are ports of the model repository's Apache-2.0
  front end and `tts_norm.py`.

EmbeddingGemma 2 (Recall, optional)
  Google DeepMind
  Gemma Terms of Use.
  Downloaded only when the user turns Recall on.
  https://huggingface.co/google/embeddinggemma-300m

llama.cpp (Recall's engine)
  The ggml-org contributors
  MIT License.
  A pinned build is downloaded from the official llama.cpp releases for Recall's
  embedding engine.
  https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp

The app also includes the following third-party software:

onnxruntime-node
  Microsoft Corporation
  MIT License.
  The ONNX runtime that loads the voice model in the main process.
  https://github.com/microsoft/onnxruntime

@titan-design/speech-g2p
  Henry Jewkes
  MIT License.
  A pure-TypeScript port of misaki's English G2P, with misaki's US lexicon data
  (Apache License 2.0), spaCy's English tokenizer rules (MIT) and compromise
  (MIT) for part-of-speech tags.
  https://github.com/HJewkes/titan-platform

CMUdict
  Carnegie Mellon University
  BSD-2-Clause.
  The pronunciation dictionary the voice front end falls back to; the copy the
  app downloads is the model repository's conversion into its phoneme alphabet.

The downloaded models' licences travel with the downloaded files. The
Apache-2.0 licence in LICENCE covers this repository's own source.
